1
00:02:02,333 --> 00:02:04,870
We don't want to buy no lino nor nothin'.

2
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:07,995
- Mr dragore, please.
- Oh, "im.

3
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:46,868
No sound, please.

4
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:49,619
After two years I find you.

5
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,240
I want the eternal light.

6
00:02:53,083 --> 00:02:54,539
You found me too late.

7
00:02:55,125 --> 00:02:56,331
It's no longer mine.

8
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:04,874
I can kill with this from
the end of the room.

9
00:03:05,083 --> 00:03:06,118
No lies, please.

10
00:03:07,625 --> 00:03:09,286
You cannot kill in england, mahmoud.

11
00:03:10,042 --> 00:03:13,114
They... they get their murderers here,
and... hang them.

12
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:15,327
I have not come alone.

13
00:03:15,458 --> 00:03:17,619
If I hang, there are others.

14
00:03:17,958 --> 00:03:21,780
The eternal light goes back to the tomb
from which you stole it.

15
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:24,620
- But I tell you, I have not got it!
- Please, I am not a child.

16
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:28,540
I... I sold it.

17
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,032
To whom did you sell it?

18
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:32,789
To professor morlant.

19
00:03:34,708 --> 00:03:36,619
That robber of the dead.

20
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:39,747
Has he sold it?

21
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:41,490
- He did not buy to sell.
- What then?

22
00:03:41,708 --> 00:03:45,030
- Like you, mahmoud. He believes.
- Believes?

23
00:03:45,417 --> 00:03:47,123
He believes that the eternal light...

24
00:03:47,167 --> 00:03:49,123
Will open for him the gates of paradise?

25
00:03:49,458 --> 00:03:50,458
Even so...

26
00:03:50,833 --> 00:03:52,713
He gave the best part
of his fortune for it.

27
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:56,166
And very soon he will know whether
or not he was right.

28
00:03:56,458 --> 00:03:57,458
What do you mean?

29
00:03:58,417 --> 00:04:00,032
Professor morlant...

30
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:01,250
Is dying!

31
00:04:03,958 --> 00:04:06,415
Then you think it will be buried with him?

32
00:04:06,542 --> 00:04:07,702
I'm sure of it.

33
00:04:08,417 --> 00:04:09,782
We have only got to wait...

34
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:11,873
Until he is dead.

35
00:04:22,375 --> 00:04:23,615
I'm near death...

36
00:04:28,083 --> 00:04:29,914
Opener of the way.

37
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,285
What's that?

38
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:14,706
Well, what is it?

39
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:15,833
Good evening.

40
00:05:16,417 --> 00:05:17,934
I happen to be staying
in the neighbourhood...

41
00:05:17,958 --> 00:05:20,758
And hearing of your master's illness,
I took the Liberty of calling.

42
00:05:21,667 --> 00:05:22,667
How is he tonight?

43
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,661
He'll never see the morning.

44
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:26,414
He hasn't asked for anyone of my cloth?

45
00:05:26,667 --> 00:05:27,667
Nor will he.

46
00:05:27,792 --> 00:05:29,282
He's set in his ways...

47
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:31,039
And they're the ways of the heathen.

48
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:32,657
I know he won't see the rector...

49
00:05:32,792 --> 00:05:36,410
But though I'm a comparative stranger, I
don't like to leave a man to die like that.

50
00:05:36,542 --> 00:05:38,282
He'll die in his own fashion...

51
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:40,870
- As he has lived.
- Still, sometimes at the end...

52
00:05:40,917 --> 00:05:42,077
Not with him.

53
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,411
He's stubborn and unbending.

54
00:05:44,542 --> 00:05:46,658
And will be so at the throne itself.

55
00:05:48,375 --> 00:05:50,161
Well, I suppose I can be of no use, then.

56
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:51,789
No manner of use.

57
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:57,167
Goodnight.

58
00:06:09,417 --> 00:06:10,532
He's asking for you.

59
00:06:13,875 --> 00:06:15,456
Where can I find mr broughton?

60
00:06:30,458 --> 00:06:31,458
Who is it?

61
00:06:31,917 --> 00:06:33,077
Come in or go out!

62
00:06:42,917 --> 00:06:45,408
You'll have to go up soon, if you
want to see him again.

63
00:06:49,958 --> 00:06:51,243
Curious house, this.

64
00:06:52,125 --> 00:06:53,125
Curious owner.

65
00:06:53,458 --> 00:06:57,781
Yes, but I suppose a great egyptologist
can't be expected to be like other people.

66
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,161
Well, he'll be like a great
many other people soon.

67
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:02,286
That's not a very sympathetic thing to say.

68
00:07:02,667 --> 00:07:04,123
I'm not a sympathetic man.

69
00:07:05,375 --> 00:07:06,375
Want a drink?

70
00:07:06,583 --> 00:07:09,780
That's, uh... across the hall, isn't it?

71
00:07:10,167 --> 00:07:11,167
I daresay.

72
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:12,833
Thanks.

73
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:25,072
Seventy-five thousand...

74
00:07:26,208 --> 00:07:31,532
September twenty-second,
nineteen thirty-one.

75
00:07:45,917 --> 00:07:47,657
Daily journal.

76
00:07:55,042 --> 00:07:56,407
Nineteen...

77
00:07:58,125 --> 00:07:59,535
Twenty-two.

78
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,661
The eternal light...

79
00:08:05,625 --> 00:08:08,332
Mine at last.

80
00:08:33,042 --> 00:08:38,287
- I want to see laing... laing.
- I'm here.

81
00:08:42,333 --> 00:08:43,914
Is the door shut?

82
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:45,333
It is.

83
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:49,119
- No listeners?
- None.

84
00:08:51,417 --> 00:08:54,079
- The curtains.
- They are drawn.

85
00:08:56,833 --> 00:08:58,539
Come nearer.

86
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,116
This man, broughton...

87
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:19,537
Watch... broughton.

88
00:09:20,417 --> 00:09:22,373
You were always suspicious.

89
00:09:22,625 --> 00:09:25,162
Have you ever trusted a living soul?

90
00:09:25,583 --> 00:09:27,164
Only fools.

91
00:09:29,875 --> 00:09:31,456
I trust you.

92
00:09:32,375 --> 00:09:35,333
Better to trust in the
spirit than in the flesh.

93
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:38,116
I put my trust...

94
00:09:39,042 --> 00:09:41,454
In my own gods.

95
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:47,326
And now... when I am dead...

96
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,206
My funeral.

97
00:09:51,458 --> 00:09:53,949
You will bury me at dusk...

98
00:09:54,958 --> 00:09:57,324
In the clothes I told you.

99
00:09:58,708 --> 00:10:01,620
You will place the figure of Anubis...

100
00:10:02,667 --> 00:10:05,409
At the west of the inner chamber.

101
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:06,625
I will.

102
00:10:08,458 --> 00:10:10,119
And on the night...

103
00:10:10,958 --> 00:10:12,573
Of the full moon...

104
00:10:15,542 --> 00:10:17,498
At the first hour...

105
00:10:19,417 --> 00:10:23,239
I will make my offering
of the eternal light...

106
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:25,660
To Anubis...

107
00:10:27,083 --> 00:10:30,280
Opener of the ways.

108
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:36,413
If I have done well in his sight...

109
00:10:38,708 --> 00:10:42,872
Those fingers will
close over the Jewel...

110
00:10:46,542 --> 00:10:51,036
And he will open to me
the gates of immortality.

111
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:55,871
The hand of a heathen image
will no come to life.

112
00:10:56,125 --> 00:11:00,915
Ahh... the bandage, the bandage.

113
00:11:40,083 --> 00:11:41,083
Look.

114
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:49,871
This... is the eternal light.

115
00:11:52,542 --> 00:11:56,364
It must rest... in my hand.

116
00:11:57,042 --> 00:12:00,864
A man will no find peace
who robs his heirs.

117
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:04,116
Bandage my hand.

118
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:06,619
The eternal light...

119
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,865
Must lie with me...

120
00:12:09,417 --> 00:12:10,953
In the tomb.

121
00:12:11,708 --> 00:12:13,824
You're afraid of me?

122
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:16,790
I'm afraid for you.

123
00:12:17,208 --> 00:12:19,449
If this should leave me...

124
00:12:20,875 --> 00:12:24,367
Then you'll have reason... to fear.

125
00:12:26,417 --> 00:12:31,957
For when the full moon strikes
the door of my tomb...

126
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:34,161
I will come back.

127
00:12:35,625 --> 00:12:36,831
You hear?

128
00:12:37,958 --> 00:12:41,405
I will come back... to kill!

129
00:12:43,708 --> 00:12:45,323
Bandage...

130
00:12:46,125 --> 00:12:47,410
My hand.

131
00:13:28,417 --> 00:13:30,874
Doctor! Doctor!

132
00:13:34,708 --> 00:13:35,708
Doctor!

133
00:13:52,292 --> 00:13:53,407
Window...

134
00:13:55,583 --> 00:13:59,371
Open... oh... oh...

135
00:14:29,375 --> 00:14:30,375
It's all over.

136
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:36,874
Make out a certificate. Heart failure.

137
00:14:41,042 --> 00:14:44,409
What was the idea of bandaging
his hand like that?

138
00:14:45,167 --> 00:14:46,452
I cannae say.

139
00:14:46,917 --> 00:14:48,953
He had many a queer fancy.

140
00:14:51,333 --> 00:14:53,619
I'll be round in the morning
to sign the certificate.

141
00:14:59,792 --> 00:15:03,990
I'll no' be leaving my master's side
til his body is laid to rest.

142
00:15:04,875 --> 00:15:05,875
Ah.

143
00:16:56,208 --> 00:16:57,208
Where are you going?

144
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,413
To feed the lamp that is to burn inside.

145
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:34,415
- It shouldn't be allowed.
- It's all wrong.

146
00:18:39,833 --> 00:18:43,701
Wait... you're leaving the key inside.

147
00:18:43,875 --> 00:18:47,868
Aye... that was another
of his queer fancies.

148
00:19:07,708 --> 00:19:13,624
When your master died, laing, I believe him to
have been possessed of a Jewel of great value.

149
00:19:14,667 --> 00:19:15,867
Do you know anything about it?

150
00:19:16,542 --> 00:19:17,542
Nothing.

151
00:19:17,792 --> 00:19:20,158
I advise you to be very careful, laing.

152
00:19:20,167 --> 00:19:21,623
I have a careful nature.

153
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:25,072
You may be putting yourself
perilously near dishonesty.

154
00:19:25,833 --> 00:19:27,698
I've seen men nearer.

155
00:19:36,292 --> 00:19:37,873
You may regret this, laing.

156
00:20:08,417 --> 00:20:09,417
Davies.

157
00:20:10,917 --> 00:20:13,659
I want you to stay here and watch
that man with the club foot.

158
00:20:14,167 --> 00:20:15,873
I'm not a detective, mr broughton.

159
00:20:15,917 --> 00:20:18,624
One more word from you, Davies,
and you're out of work.

160
00:20:19,292 --> 00:20:22,705
I have reason to believe that he has
stolen a valuable piece of property.

161
00:20:23,125 --> 00:20:24,706
He may make an effort to get rid of it.

162
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:28,405
Watch him... and telephone me at my
office if he leaves the house.

163
00:20:29,250 --> 00:20:30,250
Very good, sir.

164
00:21:08,417 --> 00:21:09,417
Harlon.

165
00:21:15,417 --> 00:21:17,533
Miss Betty harlon.

166
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,288
52 blandford street.

167
00:22:46,417 --> 00:22:47,497
Carrier!

168
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:56,708
From repson's.

169
00:22:57,333 --> 00:23:01,406
Ten shillings if you'll drive me to yaxford
station, in time to catch the five o'clock train.

170
00:23:01,458 --> 00:23:02,573
I'll oblige yer, guv'nor.

171
00:23:02,667 --> 00:23:04,623
I was going straight back, as it was.

172
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:34,072
That's a very old carpet, mr morlant, I should
be glad if you will not kick it to pieces.

173
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:36,870
I'm sorry, but when I'm angry I do kick.

174
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:38,948
Would you like to explain that?

175
00:23:39,125 --> 00:23:40,160
Yes, I intend to.

176
00:23:42,125 --> 00:23:45,325
By your own statement, miss harlon and I
are the sole heirs of professor morlant.

177
00:23:45,417 --> 00:23:47,698
We were informed neither of his death,
nor of his funeral.

178
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:52,449
Your uncle died and was buried in a certain
way, according to his wishes, which...

179
00:23:53,125 --> 00:23:54,125
Need I go on?

180
00:23:54,792 --> 00:23:58,580
Almost his last words were a
threat to return from the dead.

181
00:23:59,417 --> 00:24:00,657
In my opinion, he was mad.

182
00:24:00,958 --> 00:24:02,038
Well, that may be so.

183
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:04,059
But, miss harlon and I should
have been consulted.

184
00:24:04,083 --> 00:24:06,995
But I understood that you and
miss harlon were not on speaking terms.

185
00:24:07,042 --> 00:24:09,533
Oh, what of that? You expect quiet
at a funeral, don't you?

186
00:24:09,875 --> 00:24:11,331
Yes, I also expected...

187
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:14,180
I'm very sorry but, after all, this means
a good deal to both of us.

188
00:24:14,708 --> 00:24:17,575
- My uncle was worth about four thousand a year.
- Well, he isn't now.

189
00:24:18,417 --> 00:24:19,657
What do you mean by that?

190
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,328
He spent a good deal, you know?

191
00:24:23,417 --> 00:24:28,332
It may surprise you to know that some
time ago, he drew a cheque for £75,000.

192
00:24:28,792 --> 00:24:29,792
What for?

193
00:24:30,333 --> 00:24:31,333
I don't know.

194
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,851
You don't know? You were in charge of
all his affairs, and you don't know?

195
00:24:34,875 --> 00:24:35,875
That is what I said.

196
00:24:37,250 --> 00:24:39,866
And I advise you to look after
the tone of your voice.

197
00:24:40,333 --> 00:24:44,406
I'm not at all sure I haven't much more important
things to look after than the tone of my voice.

198
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:45,618
I don't follow you.

199
00:24:46,542 --> 00:24:48,823
I'm going to run down to earlsvale house
tomorrow morning.

200
00:24:49,875 --> 00:24:54,323
Yes, well I... I don't
think you realise the...

201
00:24:54,792 --> 00:24:56,532
Conditions that you will find there.

202
00:24:56,667 --> 00:24:59,249
- No, that's why I propose to go.
- You won't like it.

203
00:25:00,167 --> 00:25:01,327
You'll be most uncomfortable.

204
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:03,407
You don't advise me to go?

205
00:25:04,167 --> 00:25:06,783
I think you'll be making
a very big mistake.

206
00:25:08,167 --> 00:25:09,167
Then I'll go!

207
00:25:10,917 --> 00:25:11,917
Oh, by the way...

208
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:14,393
Does miss harlon know anything
about this will business?

209
00:25:14,417 --> 00:25:17,079
No doubt she will have received
a letter from me by now.

210
00:25:17,708 --> 00:25:19,494
- Do you know miss harlon?
- No.

211
00:25:20,542 --> 00:25:23,409
I propose to give myself the pleasure
of calling upon her this evening.

212
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:27,500
Hello.

213
00:25:27,917 --> 00:25:29,623
Oh, it's you, Davies. Wait a minute.

214
00:25:30,083 --> 00:25:33,155
I have a visitor here, but
I think he's just going.

215
00:25:33,458 --> 00:25:34,493
Thank you very much.

216
00:25:35,333 --> 00:25:38,040
If you're going to see miss harlon tonight,
I shall be there myself.

217
00:25:38,292 --> 00:25:41,784
No doubt you will succeed in making a
painful interview intolerable.

218
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Good afternoon.

219
00:25:44,792 --> 00:25:47,078
Your manner must help your
practice a great deal.

220
00:25:54,333 --> 00:25:55,448
Now, Davies...

221
00:26:05,667 --> 00:26:08,409
Can you direct me to
blandford street, please?

222
00:26:08,458 --> 00:26:11,825
Follow the tram lines, close on a mile
and then turn right at the church.

223
00:26:11,833 --> 00:26:13,198
I'm obliged to you.

224
00:26:41,542 --> 00:26:42,622
Oh, hello kaney.

225
00:26:43,750 --> 00:26:44,750
Ooh!

226
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:57,413
Oohh! Oh, it's good to get out of that fog.

227
00:26:57,625 --> 00:27:00,162
My dear, a most exciting
thing has happened.

228
00:27:01,083 --> 00:27:02,619
Oh, don't let it happen again!

229
00:27:02,750 --> 00:27:06,368
No - not that, that's a Chestnut.
It's this.

230
00:27:07,708 --> 00:27:09,539
It looks like a solicitor's letter.

231
00:27:09,625 --> 00:27:11,490
It's just been delivered by hand.

232
00:27:11,542 --> 00:27:12,657
Ooh, dear...

233
00:27:12,792 --> 00:27:14,123
What haven't we paid?

234
00:27:14,292 --> 00:27:16,123
I wonder if I'm going
to get a shock or not!

235
00:27:17,375 --> 00:27:19,707
Oh, kaney - that is a silly game.

236
00:27:20,875 --> 00:27:24,538
After all we've said about uncle Henry...
What do you think he's done?

237
00:27:24,708 --> 00:27:27,074
- Something nice at last?
- Well, he's dead.

238
00:27:27,792 --> 00:27:29,783
My dear, I'm sorry.

239
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,865
And his solicitor wants to see me.

240
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:33,664
My dear, I'm glad.

241
00:27:34,333 --> 00:27:35,994
He was awfully rich, wasn't he?

242
00:27:36,250 --> 00:27:38,616
Oh! He may have left you a fortune!

243
00:27:38,667 --> 00:27:41,329
- If he has, I'll buy you a private cinema.
- Oh!

244
00:27:41,792 --> 00:27:44,124
I say... when did this letter come?

245
00:27:44,583 --> 00:27:46,244
A few minutes ago. Why?

246
00:27:46,458 --> 00:27:49,165
He asked me to telephone him,
if I could see him here at six.

247
00:27:50,708 --> 00:27:53,700
You don't want to miss the chance of a
fortune, for the sake of tuppence!

248
00:27:54,083 --> 00:27:56,449
- You'd better run out and do it now.
- You're right!

249
00:29:44,417 --> 00:29:46,408
- Miss harlon?
- Yes.

250
00:30:24,083 --> 00:30:25,143
What's the matter? What's happened?

251
00:30:25,167 --> 00:30:26,873
Somebody attacked me and snatched my bag.

252
00:30:27,792 --> 00:30:31,114
- Why, good lord! It's Betty harlon.
- Ralph morlant.

253
00:30:31,792 --> 00:30:34,158
You would go and get yourself into
some kind of mix up.

254
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:36,582
- You would arrive when it's all over.
- Thank you.

255
00:30:36,875 --> 00:30:38,661
- Well, I'm going home.
- Wait a minute.

256
00:30:39,125 --> 00:30:41,161
I was on my way to see
you, strictly on business.

257
00:30:41,250 --> 00:30:43,370
Well, you wouldn't be allowed in
for any other reason.

258
00:30:43,542 --> 00:30:44,542
That's good.

259
00:31:19,875 --> 00:31:20,875
Taxi!

260
00:31:22,542 --> 00:31:24,453
Penningham garage - as quickly as possible.

261
00:31:57,250 --> 00:31:59,366
Oh, so you've brought him.

262
00:31:59,792 --> 00:32:02,659
Dear mr broughton, we're
delighted to see you.

263
00:32:02,667 --> 00:32:05,625
No, it isn't mr broughton.
It's my cousin - Ralph morlant.

264
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,413
Dear mr morlant, we're
delighted to see you.

265
00:32:09,583 --> 00:32:12,780
- Wrong again! We don't like him very much.
- Oh, don't we?

266
00:32:13,333 --> 00:32:14,664
I didn't realise.

267
00:32:15,125 --> 00:32:17,207
Well, our two families are
not on speaking terms.

268
00:32:17,333 --> 00:32:18,333
Oh, dear.

269
00:32:18,417 --> 00:32:21,497
As far as I can make out, it was started by
my late uncle as a Christmas joke.

270
00:32:21,708 --> 00:32:22,072
Oh...!

271
00:32:22,667 --> 00:32:24,749
- Won't you sit down?
- Thank you.

272
00:32:25,875 --> 00:32:28,833
But now he's dead, the trouble's all over.

273
00:32:29,167 --> 00:32:30,907
I'm not sure it hasn't just begun.

274
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:33,286
Where's mr broughton?

275
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:35,582
Oh, he won't come because
I didn't telephone.

276
00:32:35,833 --> 00:32:37,698
I nearly got throttled instead.

277
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,956
- Betty!
- There was a man with a limp.

278
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:41,865
He pushed a note into my hand.

279
00:32:42,125 --> 00:32:43,661
I just put it in my bag...

280
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,036
When somebody snatched the whole affair.

281
00:32:46,208 --> 00:32:47,208
What was in it?

282
00:32:47,625 --> 00:32:50,207
"There's something of value at earlsvale.”

283
00:32:50,792 --> 00:32:52,123
"Others are after it..."

284
00:32:52,667 --> 00:32:53,406
"So come."

285
00:32:53,542 --> 00:32:56,500
And broughton was doing everything he knew
to keep me away from there.

286
00:32:58,250 --> 00:32:59,786
There's a fox in the cover, somewhere!

287
00:33:00,917 --> 00:33:01,917
Goodbye.

288
00:33:03,125 --> 00:33:04,410
Well, why goodbye?

289
00:33:04,875 --> 00:33:06,490
I'm going down there right away.

290
00:33:06,542 --> 00:33:07,768
I'll let you know what happens.

291
00:33:07,792 --> 00:33:09,498
You're wrong - I'll let myself know.

292
00:33:09,583 --> 00:33:11,073
If you go, I go too.

293
00:33:11,583 --> 00:33:12,823
You can't do that!

294
00:33:13,333 --> 00:33:16,780
Alone in a house, with a man you're
not even on speaking terms with!

295
00:33:16,833 --> 00:33:20,075
Oh, don't be so absurd... it's not
as if I even liked him.

296
00:33:20,333 --> 00:33:22,415
If another woman was going, perhaps.

297
00:33:22,833 --> 00:33:24,664
I suppose that means you want to come too?

298
00:33:24,667 --> 00:33:26,407
Well, obviously - it's my duty.

299
00:33:26,792 --> 00:33:28,123
And suppose I object?

300
00:33:29,250 --> 00:33:31,616
I'm not so broke I can't hire a car.

301
00:33:32,292 --> 00:33:35,955
Oh, all right - you win. But
for goodness' sake, hurry!

302
00:33:49,333 --> 00:33:52,655
Girls - you must get in this as
best you can. There you are.

303
00:33:57,667 --> 00:33:58,326
You first.

304
00:33:58,542 --> 00:33:59,702
No, you - hurry up.

305
00:34:03,542 --> 00:34:07,535
- Ooh, this is an unspeakable car!
- There's no room for my legs!

306
00:34:07,583 --> 00:34:09,915
All right, all right!

307
00:34:17,917 --> 00:34:19,828
It looks as if I'll have to walk.

308
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:23,072
You might do worse... there's a grand moon.

309
00:34:23,208 --> 00:34:24,448
It's full.

310
00:35:53,083 --> 00:35:55,244
I'll see if there's a name on this gate.

311
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:02,340
No, there's nothing to
show this is the place.

312
00:36:02,375 --> 00:36:05,447
But there aren't any other
places, and I'm frozen.

313
00:36:05,958 --> 00:36:07,949
Well, it's no use going to the wrong place.

314
00:36:08,167 --> 00:36:11,047
Wait a minute, here's someone on a bike.
Hi there, cocky - wait a minute.

315
00:36:12,875 --> 00:36:13,875
Oh, hello.

316
00:36:13,917 --> 00:36:16,078
Oh, I'm awfully sorry - I didn't see
you were a parson.

317
00:36:16,083 --> 00:36:17,083
Oh, that's all right.

318
00:36:18,958 --> 00:36:20,539
- Any trouble?
- Oh, no - no.

319
00:36:20,792 --> 00:36:23,283
We just want to get to earlsvale house.

320
00:36:23,917 --> 00:36:25,077
Well, this is it.

321
00:36:25,667 --> 00:36:27,498
As a matter of fact I'm
calling there myself.

322
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:30,992
- Did you know my uncle, professor morlant?
- Oh, slightly.

323
00:36:31,458 --> 00:36:34,450
Perhaps I ought to introduce myself.
My name's hartley, Nigel hartley.

324
00:36:34,458 --> 00:36:37,825
- I'm down at raveley. The... the vicar's ill.
- How do you do?

325
00:36:38,458 --> 00:36:39,458
I'm Ralph morlant.

326
00:36:40,917 --> 00:36:42,077
This is miss harlon.

327
00:36:42,542 --> 00:36:43,531
We're the heirs of...

328
00:36:43,542 --> 00:36:48,161
- Couldn't we have the rest of the introduction indoors?
- Yes, yes - of course. You must be cold.

329
00:36:50,125 --> 00:36:53,492
- It's straight down this drive. You go along - I'll follow.
- All right.

330
00:37:20,750 --> 00:37:21,750
Here we are.

331
00:37:28,583 --> 00:37:29,993
Car'll be all right here.

332
00:37:31,667 --> 00:37:32,998
I'll show you the way.

333
00:38:23,750 --> 00:38:25,536
What a horrible house!

334
00:38:26,417 --> 00:38:28,999
I wish I was back home in bed.

335
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,615
I can hear someone coming.

336
00:38:40,208 --> 00:38:41,208
Ah!

337
00:38:44,750 --> 00:38:47,116
Well, don't stand about. Come inside.

338
00:39:20,417 --> 00:39:21,623
We'll go into the library.

339
00:39:53,833 --> 00:39:57,576
I may be old-fashioned, but I feel awkward
when I'm not introduced to people.

340
00:39:57,917 --> 00:40:00,408
I'm sorry, I forgot you didn't know
your clients by sight.

341
00:40:02,500 --> 00:40:03,535
This is miss harlon.

342
00:40:04,083 --> 00:40:05,083
How do you do?

343
00:40:05,292 --> 00:40:07,874
I was expecting a telephone
message from you.

344
00:40:08,083 --> 00:40:09,744
Oh, I was on my way to call you up...

345
00:40:10,125 --> 00:40:12,332
When the most extraordinary
thing happened.

346
00:40:15,167 --> 00:40:16,247
And this is miss kaney.

347
00:40:18,833 --> 00:40:19,833
How do you do?

348
00:40:25,625 --> 00:40:27,240
You're a surprise, broughton.

349
00:40:28,292 --> 00:40:30,908
I have a great deal of business to
clear up down here.

350
00:40:31,292 --> 00:40:34,864
This house has needed a woman
for about twenty-five years.

351
00:40:36,625 --> 00:40:38,707
Eugh! Now I've blinded myself.

352
00:40:39,792 --> 00:40:42,374
You haven't wasted much time in getting
here, mr morlant.

353
00:40:42,417 --> 00:40:44,453
No! Just a little too much perhaps?

354
00:40:45,042 --> 00:40:46,282
Whatever do you mean?

355
00:40:46,667 --> 00:40:48,578
Really! You're the rudest man alive.

356
00:40:49,083 --> 00:40:51,620
Oh, pretty pussy!

357
00:40:52,083 --> 00:40:54,290
How horrible! It's stuffed.

358
00:40:54,708 --> 00:40:56,824
I daresay you know your own business best.

359
00:40:57,083 --> 00:40:59,074
But why you should want
to bring a parson...?

360
00:40:59,292 --> 00:41:02,614
- A pure accident. We met at the gates.
- So, naturally, you brought him in.

361
00:41:02,625 --> 00:41:04,393
Broughton, I can stand a
certain amount - but no more.

362
00:41:04,417 --> 00:41:06,337
Ah, come, come. Don't let's
make a battle of it.

363
00:41:16,917 --> 00:41:18,407
- You stay here in the car.
- No!

364
00:41:19,167 --> 00:41:22,239
I shall be among the trees... watching.

365
00:41:35,083 --> 00:41:37,415
You may say I have no right to
express this opinion...

366
00:41:37,417 --> 00:41:40,784
But to my mind it's a scandalous
and disgraceful burial...

367
00:41:40,833 --> 00:41:43,040
Which may have disastrous consequences.

368
00:41:43,083 --> 00:41:46,041
It'd be very disastrous if he came
back, wouldn't it?

369
00:41:46,083 --> 00:41:47,789
I quite see mr hartley's point.

370
00:41:47,833 --> 00:41:49,744
- Yes, you make friends quickly, don't you?
- And enemies quicker.

371
00:41:49,750 --> 00:41:51,581
Need we have these childish squabbles?

372
00:41:53,083 --> 00:41:55,074
We all know that dead men don't come back.

373
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:01,707
Oh! I wish I was back home in bed!

374
00:42:02,417 --> 00:42:03,817
Hadn't somebody better answer that?

375
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,000
Certainly.

376
00:42:05,500 --> 00:42:07,616
- It's your house.
- Very well.

377
00:42:15,333 --> 00:42:16,698
I'm sorry to disturb you.

378
00:42:16,917 --> 00:42:19,283
But I was an intimate friend
of professor morlant.

379
00:42:21,333 --> 00:42:22,413
Well, you'd better come in.

380
00:42:22,625 --> 00:42:24,456
- We seem to be giving a party.
- Oh!

381
00:42:25,667 --> 00:42:26,667
Well, thank you.

382
00:42:39,333 --> 00:42:41,699
My name is aga Ben dragore.

383
00:42:41,917 --> 00:42:42,997
An Egyptian?

384
00:42:43,708 --> 00:42:44,708
An arab!

385
00:42:44,958 --> 00:42:46,698
I don't remember having heard your name.

386
00:42:47,417 --> 00:42:49,248
I did not flatter myself that you would.

387
00:42:49,625 --> 00:42:51,991
But I knew professor
morlant, some years ago.

388
00:42:52,417 --> 00:42:53,417
In Egypt.

389
00:43:02,917 --> 00:43:04,032
I heard of his death.

390
00:43:04,958 --> 00:43:06,994
And of his burial, in my own faith.

391
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:09,957
And I hoped, as I am leaving
england tomorrow...

392
00:43:10,250 --> 00:43:12,787
That I might be allowed
to visit his tomb.

393
00:43:14,042 --> 00:43:16,078
I must protest against
anything of the sort.

394
00:43:16,375 --> 00:43:19,617
Why shouldn't the poor man look
at his friend's tomb?

395
00:43:19,875 --> 00:43:21,240
I don't mind him going.

396
00:43:21,917 --> 00:43:24,989
I can't believe that you'd willingly
encourage paganism.

397
00:43:25,417 --> 00:43:27,624
The Egyptians were not pagans, sir.

398
00:43:28,542 --> 00:43:30,828
As no doubt you know miss... er...?

399
00:43:31,458 --> 00:43:32,458
Kaney.

400
00:43:33,750 --> 00:43:37,413
I think you're all being
very unkind to mr dragore.

401
00:43:37,625 --> 00:43:41,868
I don't think you people realise quite
how far morlant's queer ideas took him.

402
00:43:42,250 --> 00:43:43,786
He even believed that after his death...

403
00:43:43,792 --> 00:43:44,451
At a certain hour...

404
00:43:44,500 --> 00:43:46,866
The image of Anubis would come
to life in his tomb...

405
00:43:46,875 --> 00:43:48,081
And receive his soul.

406
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:49,535
It's horrible!

407
00:43:50,625 --> 00:43:52,240
Well, I can't see that it matters.

408
00:43:52,667 --> 00:43:55,784
After all, if that sort of mumbo-jumbo
gave him any comfort I...

409
00:43:55,792 --> 00:43:57,328
It matters a great deal.

410
00:43:57,417 --> 00:44:00,784
If my suggestion is likely to
hurt anyone's feelings...

411
00:44:01,875 --> 00:44:02,875
Please forget it.

412
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:06,788
Oh, I think that's very
sweet of you, mr dragore.

413
00:44:07,333 --> 00:44:09,870
Oh, your sympathy is more than charming.

414
00:44:11,708 --> 00:44:15,701
Well? What about a cup of coffee
after your cold drive?

415
00:44:16,042 --> 00:44:18,408
I daresay we should find
some in the kitchen.

416
00:44:19,083 --> 00:44:22,371
May I offer my services, as pantry man?

417
00:44:23,542 --> 00:44:25,453
Quite sweet of you.

418
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:30,161
Come, mr dragore.

419
00:44:32,542 --> 00:44:36,490
For sheer speed! She'll not let him
out of her sight now.

420
00:44:36,708 --> 00:44:38,414
Perhaps that's just as well.

421
00:44:40,167 --> 00:44:42,533
Come along, Betty. How about
making a fire in the library?

422
00:44:42,792 --> 00:44:43,792
Yes.

423
00:44:44,833 --> 00:44:46,915
I'm sorry there should be this
sort of atmosphere.

424
00:44:46,917 --> 00:44:49,454
After all, we're only ships
that pass in the night.

425
00:44:49,667 --> 00:44:50,667
Hmm.

426
00:44:50,708 --> 00:44:52,994
Do you want a drink, or will you pass now?

427
00:44:53,833 --> 00:44:55,073
Oh, well, thank you very much.

428
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,000
There you are.

429
00:45:16,250 --> 00:45:18,616
Well, if you build it that way there
won't be any draught.

430
00:45:19,125 --> 00:45:21,845
Oh? It'll be the only place in this house
where there isn't one then.

431
00:45:23,250 --> 00:45:26,322
Oh, don't you think you carry those
snappy retorts a trifle too far?

432
00:45:26,708 --> 00:45:29,950
And since we've met, I can't remember
you saying a kind word to anyone.

433
00:45:31,042 --> 00:45:32,042
Perhaps you're right.

434
00:45:32,708 --> 00:45:33,708
I'm sorry.

435
00:45:43,292 --> 00:45:44,327
Six cups.

436
00:45:45,417 --> 00:45:46,417
That's just...

437
00:45:47,417 --> 00:45:50,250
Just four too many - eh?

438
00:45:52,083 --> 00:45:54,074
Tell me about Egypt.

439
00:45:54,958 --> 00:45:56,869
Have you ever seen a sheikh?

440
00:45:58,750 --> 00:45:59,750
I am one!

441
00:46:07,917 --> 00:46:09,703
Oh, thank you.

442
00:46:11,417 --> 00:46:13,874
Then how should I address you?

443
00:46:14,542 --> 00:46:18,660
Oh, I'm cutting sandwiches for a sheikh!

444
00:46:18,875 --> 00:46:20,740
I don't feel quite well.

445
00:46:21,042 --> 00:46:22,407
Oh, don't be alarmed.

446
00:46:22,917 --> 00:46:25,454
We're not quite as
uncivilised as people think.

447
00:46:25,583 --> 00:46:27,915
- Oh, don't say that!
- Hmm?

448
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:31,332
Do you ride a white stallion?

449
00:46:31,458 --> 00:46:32,994
- Sometimes.
- Oh!

450
00:46:33,333 --> 00:46:35,790
Down the path of the moon.

451
00:46:36,167 --> 00:46:40,115
The noble animal, plunging and
frothing at the nostrils...

452
00:46:40,417 --> 00:46:43,784
Til it founders at your
feet, faithful unto death.

453
00:46:43,958 --> 00:46:45,243
Well, not very often.

454
00:46:45,625 --> 00:46:47,991
You see, it's rather too expensive.

455
00:46:48,708 --> 00:46:50,073
Oh, I know it's not your fault...

456
00:46:50,167 --> 00:46:51,726
We were taught to
hate one another, but...

457
00:46:51,750 --> 00:46:53,550
Good lord, you don't think I
hate you, do you?

458
00:46:53,750 --> 00:46:56,332
Well, I can't somehow feel I'm
your dearest friend.

459
00:46:57,167 --> 00:46:59,127
You never did have a great deal
of sense, did you?

460
00:46:59,375 --> 00:47:00,410
Oh, that's nice.

461
00:47:03,250 --> 00:47:03,955
Ralph?

462
00:47:04,250 --> 00:47:07,083
I've a woman's intuition that you and
I are up against things.

463
00:47:08,167 --> 00:47:09,407
Yes, I'm pretty sure we are.

464
00:47:09,583 --> 00:47:11,869
Well, then... let's cut the quarrelling.

465
00:47:12,167 --> 00:47:14,203
Shoulder to shoulder, eh? All right.

466
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,197
Partners.

467
00:47:16,333 --> 00:47:18,198
- Partners.
- Ha!

468
00:47:32,375 --> 00:47:33,990
Well, what a wonderful night.

469
00:47:34,500 --> 00:47:35,740
It's a full moon.

470
00:47:52,042 --> 00:47:54,704
Scared of a dead man in his tomb?

471
00:47:55,667 --> 00:47:57,282
Shame on yourself.

472
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:04,369
Are you a child that your knee should
rattle at the talk of a madman?

473
00:48:07,750 --> 00:48:09,991
Look your enemy in the face.

474
00:48:10,875 --> 00:48:13,457
It's the fear of the big door has got you.

475
00:48:13,708 --> 00:48:17,075
And will hold you fast
'til you stare it down.

476
00:48:23,625 --> 00:48:25,240
Do dead men walk?

477
00:48:26,708 --> 00:48:30,405
I'm no' thinking a dead man will
cross my path tonight.

478
00:49:14,500 --> 00:49:16,582
Arrrgh!

479
00:50:01,917 --> 00:50:02,917
Urrgh!

480
00:51:24,792 --> 00:51:27,534
Oh! I was dreaming.

481
00:51:28,083 --> 00:51:29,323
Now I will show you...

482
00:51:29,458 --> 00:51:31,323
How we make coffee in the desert...

483
00:51:31,542 --> 00:51:33,157
Underneath the stars.

484
00:51:34,625 --> 00:51:36,911
You don't make it yourself, do you?

485
00:51:37,167 --> 00:51:39,158
No, of course not.

486
00:51:39,792 --> 00:51:45,162
A circassian slave - lovely as sin -
cooks it for us, kneeling.

487
00:51:45,417 --> 00:51:48,159
- And if it is not to our liking...
- I know!

488
00:51:49,333 --> 00:51:51,824
She's stripped to the waist...

489
00:51:52,458 --> 00:51:56,201
And lashed for miles across the Sahara.

490
00:51:56,458 --> 00:52:00,406
Where she is finally eaten - by locusts.
And rightly.

491
00:52:01,792 --> 00:52:06,161
Now, take this canister and
do exactly as I tell you.

492
00:52:06,333 --> 00:52:07,618
Oh!

493
00:52:08,250 --> 00:52:09,990
And if I fail?

494
00:52:10,125 --> 00:52:12,787
The Yorkshire moors are just behind us.

495
00:52:14,875 --> 00:52:15,875
Now.

496
00:52:16,250 --> 00:52:17,615
Six spoonfuls.

497
00:52:19,417 --> 00:52:20,417
One!

498
00:52:23,708 --> 00:52:24,993
Two!

499
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:30,000
Three!

500
00:52:32,167 --> 00:52:33,167
Four!

501
00:52:34,708 --> 00:52:35,708
Five!

502
00:52:44,875 --> 00:52:48,663
Get off you!
Take your arms away from...

503
00:52:51,250 --> 00:52:52,956
What's the matter with you?

504
00:52:53,042 --> 00:52:54,407
Are you mad, eh?

505
00:53:01,167 --> 00:53:02,998
What was the matter with him?

506
00:53:03,333 --> 00:53:05,119
- Was it drink?
- No!

507
00:53:05,792 --> 00:53:06,792
Terror!

508
00:53:07,042 --> 00:53:09,283
- Stark terror!
- Oooh!

509
00:53:09,500 --> 00:53:11,286
Then I've caught it!

510
00:53:11,708 --> 00:53:12,788
You stay here.

511
00:53:13,708 --> 00:53:15,323
I'll look after him.

512
00:53:15,667 --> 00:53:19,410
If you must look after somebody,
why look further?

513
00:53:19,542 --> 00:53:20,542
Eh?

514
00:53:21,375 --> 00:53:22,535
Come on, then.

515
00:53:28,583 --> 00:53:29,583
Ralph!

516
00:53:29,625 --> 00:53:31,456
That limp. I'd swear to it anywhere.

517
00:53:47,167 --> 00:53:48,282
That's the man!

518
00:53:53,458 --> 00:53:57,018
- Look here, did you give a note to this young lady?
- Gather up your things and get out of here!

519
00:53:57,042 --> 00:53:59,408
The master... I've seen him!!!

520
00:54:09,125 --> 00:54:10,365
Who screamed?

521
00:54:10,625 --> 00:54:11,625
I did!

522
00:54:11,708 --> 00:54:15,656
That's the last time I'll ever try to make
coffee in a strange house.

523
00:54:15,833 --> 00:54:18,870
- That man with the limp - who was he?
- Laing.

524
00:54:19,542 --> 00:54:20,873
Your uncle's servant.

525
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:23,286
Well, he seemed mad to me.

526
00:54:33,083 --> 00:54:34,083
Yes.

527
00:54:34,833 --> 00:54:36,494
And probably dangerous.

528
00:54:37,417 --> 00:54:40,018
You others had better go into the library.
I'll have a word with him.

529
00:54:40,042 --> 00:54:41,202
Yes, come along.

530
00:54:41,458 --> 00:54:43,198
Mr broughton understands the man.

531
00:54:58,250 --> 00:55:00,832
It would do no harm to warn
my man to stand by.

532
00:55:00,917 --> 00:55:01,917
Your man?

533
00:55:02,083 --> 00:55:05,371
- Is he a sheikh, too?
- No, no - he's a chauffeur.

534
00:55:05,583 --> 00:55:07,164
He's outside now, with my car.

535
00:55:11,875 --> 00:55:13,661
You're not leaving us, are you?

536
00:55:15,917 --> 00:55:17,999
My dear lady.

537
00:55:26,875 --> 00:55:30,447
Not a very courageous
person, our foreign friend.

538
00:55:30,625 --> 00:55:32,456
You think he's run away?!

539
00:55:33,000 --> 00:55:34,000
Absurd!

540
00:55:34,750 --> 00:55:36,615
I'd like to see you riding your bicycle...

541
00:55:36,625 --> 00:55:40,322
With a circassian slave, lovely
as sin, across the handlebars!

542
00:55:40,583 --> 00:55:43,450
- What on earth are you talking about?
- Now listen, good people.

543
00:55:43,583 --> 00:55:44,493
"Good people?”

544
00:55:44,542 --> 00:55:47,382
Don't you think perhaps we are allowing
this thing to get on our nerves?

545
00:55:47,417 --> 00:55:50,830
Don't you think perhaps if we took
a grip on our self-control...

546
00:55:50,833 --> 00:55:52,323
Now listen, good parson.

547
00:55:52,833 --> 00:55:56,075
This is our show, and our nerves are
probably just as good as the next man's.

548
00:55:56,542 --> 00:55:58,407
So keep that sort of talk for your pulpit.

549
00:55:58,500 --> 00:55:58,955
Ralph!

550
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:01,707
Oh, well, of course, I've no wish
to interfere where I'm not wanted.

551
00:56:01,792 --> 00:56:04,204
Then don't. This is not a Sunday school.

552
00:56:09,708 --> 00:56:11,994
After that, I think I can say "good night".

553
00:56:12,625 --> 00:56:13,785
As you please.

554
00:56:19,167 --> 00:56:20,782
Well, I'm sorry I was offensive.

555
00:56:20,792 --> 00:56:21,372
Good night.

556
00:56:21,458 --> 00:56:24,996
Oh, well, the tongue is an
unruly member - is it not?

557
00:56:25,167 --> 00:56:26,577
- Yes.
- Yes...

558
00:56:35,625 --> 00:56:37,581
I was tempted.

559
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:42,072
I was tempted, but I did not fall.

560
00:56:52,583 --> 00:56:54,369
I did not fall.

561
00:56:54,958 --> 00:56:56,368
The thing's safe.

562
00:56:56,667 --> 00:56:58,373
I swear it.

563
00:57:02,792 --> 00:57:05,499
When you told me you'd come
back from the grave...

564
00:57:05,833 --> 00:57:07,494
How could I believe you?

565
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,662
I never knew such things could be.

566
00:57:47,375 --> 00:57:48,375
No!

567
00:57:50,583 --> 00:57:51,993
Oh...! Arrgh!

568
00:57:52,708 --> 00:57:58,829
I have no' got it. I have no' got it!
The girl - she has it!

569
00:57:59,000 --> 00:58:00,456
I swear it!

570
00:58:01,625 --> 00:58:03,206
Oh! Oh!

571
00:58:27,333 --> 00:58:28,914
What on earth's the matter with you?

572
00:58:29,042 --> 00:58:30,703
You look as if you've seen a ghost.

573
00:58:31,250 --> 00:58:32,285
I have!

574
00:58:34,083 --> 00:58:35,789
I saw morlant...

575
00:58:35,875 --> 00:58:38,537
As plainly as I see you.

576
00:58:39,625 --> 00:58:41,365
I'm going to mix meself a drink.

577
00:58:50,042 --> 00:58:52,249
Betty? Just a minute.

578
00:58:55,000 --> 00:58:56,000
Well?

579
00:58:56,792 --> 00:58:59,329
I've an idea they're trying to scare us
out of this house.

580
01:00:06,542 --> 01:00:08,703
Now, there's no use blinding
ourselves to the facts.

581
01:00:08,875 --> 01:00:10,911
There must be something
pretty big at stake.

582
01:00:11,083 --> 01:00:13,165
Something that depends
on getting rid of us?

583
01:00:14,083 --> 01:00:15,163
That's how it looks to me.

584
01:00:16,042 --> 01:00:17,248
Well, what are we going to do?

585
01:01:34,167 --> 01:01:35,167
Who's there?

586
01:01:41,458 --> 01:01:43,893
- Betty, I'm going down to that tomb to find out whether...
- But...

587
01:01:43,917 --> 01:01:46,717
It's the only way we've got of finding
out what's going on around here.

588
01:01:46,833 --> 01:01:49,540
Well, I don't want to be left here
alone. Can I come too?

589
01:01:50,750 --> 01:01:52,270
There's nothing wrong with your nerve.

590
01:01:52,625 --> 01:01:53,625
Come on.

591
01:02:04,167 --> 01:02:06,158
I'll put on a pullover
and some thicker shoes.

592
01:02:06,208 --> 01:02:07,208
All right.

593
01:02:07,667 --> 01:02:08,782
- Is this yours?
- Yes.

594
01:02:09,333 --> 01:02:10,573
I'll keep an eye on broughton.

595
01:02:25,500 --> 01:02:28,900
Well, I'd think you've every chance of seeing
things if you lower scotch at that pace.

596
01:03:40,083 --> 01:03:41,083
Oh!

597
01:03:47,625 --> 01:03:48,625
Oh...!

598
01:05:17,542 --> 01:05:21,410
Mr dragore! Mr dragore! Mr dragore!

599
01:05:22,000 --> 01:05:23,331
Mr dragore!! I

600
01:05:24,042 --> 01:05:25,327
oh! There you are!

601
01:05:26,042 --> 01:05:27,327
Oh, mr dragore!

602
01:05:27,583 --> 01:05:28,823
I'll come up to you!

603
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:34,831
Wait. I'll come down.

604
01:05:40,917 --> 01:05:41,576
What do you want?

605
01:05:41,875 --> 01:05:44,457
- There was somebody in the library!
- Who?

606
01:05:44,833 --> 01:05:45,833
I don't know.

607
01:05:46,458 --> 01:05:48,073
The door... it shut!

608
01:05:48,417 --> 01:05:50,408
- It shut! I...
- Don't scream.

609
01:05:50,625 --> 01:05:52,911
Oh! That's what I need.

610
01:05:53,167 --> 01:05:56,739
The command in your wonderful voice.

611
01:06:00,417 --> 01:06:01,417
Come with me!

612
01:06:02,458 --> 01:06:05,416
I think you've gone far enough
with your insinuations.

613
01:06:05,417 --> 01:06:07,408
Yes, and I may go a great deal farther.

614
01:06:10,083 --> 01:06:11,283
What is it? What's the matter?

615
01:06:11,500 --> 01:06:13,786
I've seen him.

616
01:06:19,500 --> 01:06:22,242
Now perhaps you'll believe what I told you?

617
01:06:22,458 --> 01:06:24,138
Get me a glass of water quickly, will you?

618
01:07:26,000 --> 01:07:28,707
Thanks. I wasn't hurt - only frightened.

619
01:07:30,333 --> 01:07:32,413
Broughton - see if you can find
miss kaney, will you?

620
01:07:37,042 --> 01:07:40,614
It's wonderful to be with
a man who isn't afraid.

621
01:07:40,667 --> 01:07:41,667
I am afraid.

622
01:07:41,792 --> 01:07:45,455
You, who've ridden
bare-backed over the desert?

623
01:07:46,083 --> 01:07:48,963
If you don't stop chattering, I'm afraid
I shall have a knife in my back.

624
01:07:49,625 --> 01:07:51,866
But when I'm with you I have to talk.

625
01:07:52,208 --> 01:07:54,665
It comes, like poetry.

626
01:07:55,417 --> 01:07:56,827
Are you prepared to obey me?

627
01:07:57,583 --> 01:07:58,823
In anything.

628
01:07:59,458 --> 01:08:01,039
Then... close your eyes.

629
01:08:01,500 --> 01:08:04,037
And don't speak for ten seconds.

630
01:08:49,417 --> 01:08:50,782
We all panic sometimes.

631
01:08:50,875 --> 01:08:53,582
- I felt his hands on me.
- That's why I know it was no ghost.

632
01:08:53,792 --> 01:08:54,998
It was no ghost.

633
01:08:56,708 --> 01:08:58,039
Look at the clock.

634
01:08:58,208 --> 01:08:59,869
It's nearing the hour.

635
01:09:00,167 --> 01:09:02,408
I know where you'll find him now.

636
01:09:02,833 --> 01:09:04,414
He's gone back to the tomb.

637
01:09:04,792 --> 01:09:06,783
To his heathen gods.

638
01:09:08,708 --> 01:09:10,188
Then you and I will follow him there.

639
01:09:10,417 --> 01:09:11,417
Wait a minute.

640
01:09:12,125 --> 01:09:15,413
- What's his doctor's telephone number?
- Yaxford 72.

641
01:10:21,208 --> 01:10:22,208
Look!

642
01:10:22,292 --> 01:10:23,782
The door's open and there's a light.

643
01:10:24,042 --> 01:10:25,248
I'll go no nearer.

644
01:10:25,417 --> 01:10:26,873
I'll go no nearer.

645
01:10:29,708 --> 01:10:31,323
I can see a shadow moving.

646
01:10:31,500 --> 01:10:32,990
I'll go no nearer!

647
01:10:33,083 --> 01:10:34,163
Well then, go back.

648
01:10:36,708 --> 01:10:37,708
What about it, Betty?

649
01:10:38,625 --> 01:10:39,625
Do we go on?

650
01:10:40,750 --> 01:10:41,750
Yes, of course.

651
01:10:43,708 --> 01:10:44,708
Thought you'd say that.

652
01:11:42,458 --> 01:11:43,914
Oh...!

653
01:11:44,917 --> 01:11:47,374
No...

654
01:11:58,375 --> 01:11:59,375
Aieeeel!!

655
01:12:38,500 --> 01:12:39,500
Look!

656
01:12:52,167 --> 01:12:53,167
Hartley!

657
01:12:53,292 --> 01:12:55,408
So, you're not a parson.
Just a dirty crook!

658
01:13:00,375 --> 01:13:02,661
You'd better get out of my way.

659
01:13:03,167 --> 01:13:04,167
Your hand, eh?

660
01:13:04,708 --> 01:13:05,914
So, that's how it was done.

661
01:13:07,583 --> 01:13:10,325
- I wouldn't come any nearer.
- I don't have to!

662
01:13:17,833 --> 01:13:18,288
Look!

663
01:13:18,667 --> 01:13:19,747
If you please!

664
01:13:19,917 --> 01:13:21,077
Thank you. Come on now.

665
01:14:35,083 --> 01:14:36,083
Go!

666
01:14:43,417 --> 01:14:46,178
- Come on, it's too late. Are you badly hurt?
- No, no - it's nothing.

667
01:14:47,417 --> 01:14:48,417
Come and sit down.

668
01:14:49,542 --> 01:14:50,542
Where's the key?

669
01:14:50,625 --> 01:14:51,625
He threw it away.

670
01:15:01,458 --> 01:15:03,658
When I phoned the doctor I told
him to bring the police.

671
01:15:04,125 --> 01:15:05,365
They ought to find us somehow.

672
01:15:05,667 --> 01:15:08,864
Why, even if they do come, how can
they break down that door?

673
01:15:13,792 --> 01:15:14,872
They'll find a way.

674
01:15:19,875 --> 01:15:20,875
I'll make a bandage.

675
01:15:30,250 --> 01:15:32,582
The doctor in charge didn't
understand the case.

676
01:15:33,292 --> 01:15:35,328
- I'm afraid of catalepsy.
- Meaning?

677
01:15:35,500 --> 01:15:37,331
Morlant was buried alive.

678
01:15:38,250 --> 01:15:40,036
Oh, mr dragore!

679
01:15:40,375 --> 01:15:41,535
What were those shots?

680
01:15:42,000 --> 01:15:44,457
- Out of my way.
- Where are the others?

681
01:15:44,750 --> 01:15:46,070
Leave me alone!

682
01:15:47,625 --> 01:15:51,823
Ooh! Oh! Oooh!

683
01:16:08,417 --> 01:16:10,408
I rather thought you might
be leaving in a hurry...

684
01:16:10,417 --> 01:16:12,777
With something in your pocket
that doesn't belong to you.

685
01:16:13,583 --> 01:16:14,698
Hand it over.

686
01:16:16,250 --> 01:16:17,250
You win!

687
01:16:27,500 --> 01:16:28,500
That woman!

688
01:16:28,792 --> 01:16:29,497
There she is!

689
01:16:29,625 --> 01:16:30,159
Come now.

690
01:16:30,292 --> 01:16:33,204
Oh, you put down that gun, you fool!
I tell you, she's got it

691
01:16:37,542 --> 01:16:38,542
come on, man.

692
01:16:48,208 --> 01:16:49,208
Stop!

693
01:16:49,958 --> 01:16:51,539
Now, miss kaney - if you please.

694
01:16:51,583 --> 01:16:53,119
I don't think so.

695
01:16:53,250 --> 01:16:54,456
You fool.

696
01:16:54,708 --> 01:16:56,869
If either of you two horrible men...

697
01:16:57,083 --> 01:16:58,163
So much as move...

698
01:16:58,458 --> 01:16:59,458
In it goes.

699
01:16:59,542 --> 01:17:01,018
But you don't know the value of that Jewel.

700
01:17:01,042 --> 01:17:03,624
I don't care for the value. It'll go!

701
01:17:05,333 --> 01:17:06,448
And if you shoot...

702
01:17:06,583 --> 01:17:07,663
I'lll go with it.

703
01:17:08,625 --> 01:17:09,625
I mean it.

704
01:17:10,250 --> 01:17:11,490
Down thirty feet.

705
01:17:12,083 --> 01:17:18,329
And about sixty feet of water, and,
and... and then, Australia.

706
01:17:20,875 --> 01:17:22,411
Well, I can't see to tie this.

707
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:24,536
That light seems much lower.

708
01:17:42,417 --> 01:17:45,534
Hartley! Quick, come on - get up.
Get him out of here.

709
01:17:47,292 --> 01:17:48,292
Right.

710
01:17:51,583 --> 01:17:54,074
- The door! The door!
- It's shut!

711
01:17:55,792 --> 01:17:59,159
The flames - they mustn't reach the door!

712
01:18:14,167 --> 01:18:15,953
It's no good. You can't breathe in there.

713
01:18:19,125 --> 01:18:20,240
The cartridge.

714
01:18:22,375 --> 01:18:25,082
It's here. If only...

715
01:18:27,125 --> 01:18:28,331
If only...

716
01:18:32,250 --> 01:18:33,911
I've had enough of this, miss kaney.

717
01:18:34,500 --> 01:18:36,582
Supposing I'm ready to
shoot, and take the risk?

718
01:18:36,875 --> 01:18:39,742
You'd be taking a bigger
risk than you think.

719
01:18:40,958 --> 01:18:42,289
I'll take that gun, thank you.

720
01:18:42,333 --> 01:18:43,539
- Now look here!
- That'll do.

721
01:18:44,042 --> 01:18:45,373
Now, what's the trouble?

722
01:18:45,625 --> 01:18:46,625
This.

723
01:18:47,000 --> 01:18:48,240
They're after it.

724
01:18:48,375 --> 01:18:49,535
All of them.

725
01:18:49,792 --> 01:18:51,532
It belongs...

726
01:18:53,542 --> 01:18:54,782
I'll carry her to the house.

727
01:19:06,125 --> 01:19:07,125
Get back!

728
01:19:07,542 --> 01:19:09,407
Get to that corner!

